# LoomDB golden format fixtures — format v1.
#
# GENERATED. Do not edit by hand, and do not regenerate to make a test
# pass: a diff here is an ON-DISK FORMAT CHANGE, and for a storage engine
# that is data loss. See docs/design/serialization-format.md (issue #50).
#
# These are the bytes bincode 1.3.3 produces with its default settings:
#   * integers fixed-width and little-endian, never varint
#   * every length prefix a bare u64 (8 bytes), for any size
#   * enum discriminants a u32 of the variant's DECLARATION INDEX
#   * Option a one-byte tag; bool one byte
#   * structs a bare concatenation — no field names, no count, no type tag
#
# To ADD a case (never to bless a diff):
#   LOOMDB_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test --test golden_format

